  "rule": "On a colour-2 background scattered with colour-4 cells, every 4-cell whose four orthogonal neighbours are also 4 is the centre of a plus sign; recolour that centre and its four arms to 8 and leave every other cell unchanged.",
  "scope": "Supported: grids 8..30 per side (non-square allowed); 1..9+ latent plus centres at pairwise Chebyshev distance >= 3 (pluses never share cells, as in all originals); four constructive scene styles \u2014 random scatter with near-plus fragments (broken pluses, bars, blocks, corners, diagonals), gapped grid lines with pluses at a subset of intersections (test-like), rectangular blobs with pluses embedded in larger 4-shapes and diagonal attachments (train 3-like), and periodic tilings whose motif contains one or two pluses (train 2-like). Deliberately not supported: alternative background/ink/highlight colours (2/4/8 are fixed in every original pair), overlapping or adjacent pluses, grids with zero pluses (every sample is non-identity), and multi-colour inks.",
  "constraints": [
    "Background colour 2 is always the strict majority (ink < 45% of cells) so the solver's most-common-colour background detection matches.",
    "Intended plus centres are interior and pairwise Chebyshev distance >= 3, so no two pluses share cells and the painting order is irrelevant.",
    "After construction, _enforce guarantees the intended centres are the only cells with all four orthogonal neighbours in colour 4; unintended pluses are broken by blanking a cell that belongs to no intended plus (always available given the separation invariant).",
    "In the periodic style the motif is repaired on a torus so the tiling stays exactly periodic and only pluses fully inside the grid count as centres.",
    "Colour 8 never appears in an input; the output differs from the input in exactly 5 cells per plus.",
    "Explicit fixture forms run the same check in strict mode and raise rather than silently repairing."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Colours 2/4/8 are fixed; no colour variation is generated because every original pair uses exactly these colours.",
    "The test fixture is replayed via input_grid (its ~200 ink cells are impractical to list as coordinates); the centres are passed explicitly and verified in strict mode, so the output is still painted from latent centres rather than solved.",
    "The scene repair step uses the same local 3x3 test as the solver, but only as a validity enforcement that blanks unintended cells; outputs are always rendered from the latent centre list.",
    "Big rectangles in blob mode acquire punched holes during repair, so solid 3x3+ blocks never survive intact.",
    "Pluses are never adjacent or overlapping, which is consistent with all originals but excludes that edge case."
  ],
